From eeca35866fb780a45cad874efb55673588287ca5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cameron Basham <cambash23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:12:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 107/108] cuda roce: the one-shot RoCE all-gather at any world
 on a mesh (four Sparks on a switch), with a connect probe

roce.zig and roce_gather.cu were written for two ranks (Gather.init refused world != 2, Group.openRoce never asked),
so at TP=4 every one of a decode verify call's ~90 small all-gathers (16 KiB a rank: rows x hidden x 4 bytes) rode NCCL
Ring LL/LL128, 30-50 us each: gather_a + gather_b = 4.7 ms of a 28.3 ms call, measured with TF_GLM_PROF=1 on four GB10s
behind a MikroTik CRS804 (NCCL 2.30, two RoCE devices a Spark, every pair of ranks on both /24s). The two-rank path did
the same exchange in 10.4 us at 4 KiB and 17.4 us at 64 KiB against NCCL's 12.3 / 51.5.

The design generalised: a rank's peers are the other ranks in rank order (peerIndex / senderOf); every rank opens one RC
queue pair a peer an HCA (Hca.qp[peer]) and the region is recv[slot][world - 1][slot_bytes], flags[slot][world - 1][hca],
send[slot], ctrl. post() writes the shard's stripe on each HCA to every peer on this rank's queue pair toward it, the flag
behind it on the same queue pair; the kernel's thread tid < (world - 1) * n_hca waits for flag [slot][tid / n_hca][tid %
n_hca] and every block copies its own shard and each peer's stripes into the output slot of the sender's rank, the layout
ncclAllGather gives. The blob exchange and both verdicts cross the group's NCCL communicator as all-gathers (Group.gather
already takes N ranks) instead of the two-rank swap; the cap is the minimum over every rank's. fits(), TF_ROCE,
TF_ROCE_MAX_KB, TF_ROCE_HCA and TF_ROCE_GID_INDEX are unchanged. At world 2 (one peer) every offset, every address a NIC
writes and every byte the kernel moves is the two-rank design's, so two Sparks keep their bits and their speed (a test
pins the layout to the old formula).

Fail closed on a fabric a ring cannot carry: the RC transitions succeed whether or not a cable reaches the peer, so after
every rank reports its queue pairs in RTS (one all-gather), each rank RDMA-writes a token to every peer on every HCA and
waits for its writes' completions and every peer's token (about 5 s); a far rank on a ring of four ends in a
retry-exhausted completion or a missing token, and every rank then refuses with error.PeerUnreachable and a REFUSE TF_ROCE
line naming the rank (set TF_ROCE=0 there), before any weight loads and instead of a kernel spinning at the first gather.
The proxy thread starts only after the probe, so no completion queue is shared between threads. max_world is 8.

The launch is unchanged: a plain stream-ordered launch after the kernel that writes its input, so the PDL chains of the
decode path (glm_mm_reduce, the hc chain, the p2p gather) are untouched; the RoCE kernel is never a dependent launch.

Exactness: an all-gather is a data move. Every rank's bytes land in the output slot of its rank, as before and as NCCL
lays them; nothing is summed or rounded, so the verified tokens cannot change (hashes fab1d3b6894b / e71492bf766b on the
recipe's acc.py harness, Ablit checkpoint, greedy, must repeat).

Tests: roce.zig pins the two-rank layout, the four-rank slot and flag placement (no overlap, sender's rank order, both
sides agree on every peer number), the cap over four ranks and the fabric contract (a mesh of four reaches every rank, a
ring of four leaves rank r without rank r + 2, two on a cable are neighbours); cuda_ranks_test runs the same contract on
its fake Fabric. `tf-cuda-test roce-gather <rank> [world]` is the microbench on real ranks (NCCL_COMM_ID): every size up to
the cap and past it against ncclAllGather byte for byte, a captured graph replayed 64 times, 3,000 mixed-size calls (16 /
32 / 64 KiB a rank, tiny ones between) each compared with NCCL's rows, then the time a call of each path at 4 to 64 KiB;
its RESULT line carries the recipe's GO gate: at most 25 us a call at 32 KiB and zero mismatches. Not yet run on hardware
(this change was written without a Zig toolchain or a Spark at hand): the gate decides before any ROCE=on boot.
